Fix the race that freezes every cmd[update:N] label on the lock screen.

CAsyncResourceManager::enqueue() hands the resource to the gatherer thread on
its first line and attaches the `finished` listener on its last. The gatherer
is a single worker that wakes on enqueue, calls render() and emits `finished`
immediately -- so for a resource that renders fast (any label whose command
returns promptly, which is every one of ours) the emit can land before the main
thread reaches listenStatic(). An emit with no listeners is dropped, not
queued.

Nothing then observes that the resource is ready: onResourceFinished() is never
scheduled for that id, the widget's onAssetUpdate() never runs, and
CLabel::m_pendingResource stays true forever. Every later tick of that label
takes the early return at the top of CLabel::onTimerUpdate() and logs "Trying
to update label, but a resource is still pending! Skipping update." The label
is frozen at whatever it last rendered for the rest of the lock, which is how a
lock screen ends up showing 05:12 at noon -- one observed run logged 29,532 of
those warnings across a single 6h50m lock.

It is a race, so it bites per-request and a few seconds in rather than at
startup: on that run the clock (update:1000) and the faillock label
(update:5000) both lost it while the date label (update:60000) did not.

Registering the listener -- and recording the resource in m_resources, which
onResourceFinished() looks the id up in -- before the handoff closes the
window. There is no symmetric hazard: the callback only schedules a 0ms timer,
and the main thread cannot process it until it has returned from enqueue().

Upstream: https://github.com/hyprwm/hyprlock/issues/1071 (open as of
2026-09-30, affects 0.9.5, 0.9.6 and main; the reorder below is the fix the
report proposes). DROP THIS PATCH once nixpkgs carries a hyprlock that does it
itself -- tests/hyprlock-pending-race.sh fails the moment that happens and
names what to delete.

--- a/src/renderer/AsyncResourceManager.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer/AsyncResourceManager.cpp
@@ -254,8 +254,6 @@
 }
 
 void CAsyncResourceManager::enqueue(ResourceID resourceID, const ASP<IAsyncResource>& resource, const AWP<IWidget>& widget) {
-    m_gatherer.enqueue(resource);
-
     m_resourcesMutex.lock();
     if (m_resources.contains(resourceID))
         Log::logger->log(Log::ERR, "Resource already enqueued! This is a bug.");
@@ -275,6 +273,11 @@
             },
             (void*)resourceID);
     });
+
+    // Hand the resource over last: the gatherer thread renders it and emits
+    // `finished` as soon as it is enqueued, and an emit with no listener
+    // attached is simply dropped.
+    m_gatherer.enqueue(resource);
 }
 
 void CAsyncResourceManager::onResourceFinished(ResourceID id) {
